	(text "Start up flow:\n\n1. Power button press (boost enable with default 5V) or adaptor plugged in (default 5V), AON_5V_OR_HV rises to 5V\n2. Always-on 3V3 buck supplies power to STM32 MCU\n3. STM32 checks for battery state, holds boost enable if battery healthy\n4. Enable charging (switch on charge power path and charge enable) if adapter plugged in\n5. Check voltage on CC lines for custom divider voltage\n6. Enable MAINBOARD power (5V) to power the MCU on the other end\n7. Verify device over I2C with SBU pins (Other side is ESP32C6 which has GPIO matrix for I2C pin inversion)\n8. Shut down MAINBOARD power, raise boost voltage to 9V and adaptor negotiation voltage to 12V or 15V.\n9. Check CC again, then enable MAINBOARD power\n10. Turn on 5V buck converter for USB port power\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 39.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 194 194 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "90823db8-a6e7-48dc-a8a3-641451f0c39e")
	)
